    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Inducement shares issued by the Issuer to SportsAlert Media, LLC as consideration for loans made under the Issuer's Promissory Notes dated April 10, 2026 ($27,500; 2,750,000 shares before the Issuer's 1-for-250 reverse stock split effective June 12, 2026, or 11,000 shares after the split) and May 19, 2026 ($5,000; 500,000 shares before the split, or 2,000 shares after). No separate cash consideration was paid for the shares.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Issued by the Issuer on May 27, 2026 under the Credit Card Facility Agreement dated April 15, 2026 (executed April 23, 2026) among Sugar Auto Parts, Inc., the reporting person and Christopher Davenport: 6,000 shares (1,500,000 shares before the reverse stock split) upon execution and 6,000 shares (1,500,000 shares before the split) upon a default under the facility. The price reflects the $9,600 value of the shares as reported in the Issuer's Form 10-K for fiscal 2026.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Held by SportsAlert Media, LLC, of which the reporting person is the managing member and sole owner. Includes 80,000 shares (20,000,000 shares before the reverse stock split) reported on the reporting person's Form 3 filed October 24, 2025.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Held by Mammoth Crest Capital, LLC (&quot;MCC&quot;), which is owned 50% by the reporting person and 50% by Barrett Evans, each a managing member. The reporting person disclaims beneficial ownership of the securities held by MCC except to the extent of his pecuniary interest therein. MCC's 2,000,000 shares of Common Stock (500,000,000 shares before the Issuer's 1-for-250 reverse stock split effective June 12, 2026) and 1,250 shares of Series C Preferred Stock were acquired June 13, 2025 and were reported on the reporting person's Form 3 filed October 24, 2025.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">Each share of Series B Convertible Preferred Stock (stated value $100) is convertible at the holder's option, at any time, into the number of shares of Common Stock having a value of $100 based on the closing price of the Common Stock on the trading day before conversion. The conversion price and number of underlying shares therefore vary; based on the $0.08 closing price on October 14, 2026, the 750 shares would convert into approximately 937,500 shares of Common Stock. The Series B Preferred Stock is exercisable immediately and has no expiration date.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F6">Issued by the Issuer on December 8, 2025 as compensation, pursuant to a resolution of the Issuer's Board of Directors dated October 5, 2025, for no cash consideration. Exempt under Rule 16b-3(d).</footnote>
        <footnote id="F7">Convertible at the holder's option at any time into Common Stock at the lesser of (i) 80% of the per-share price paid in a Qualified Transaction (a priced equity financing of at least $1,000,000 with unaffiliated investors) and (ii) a valuation-cap price equal to $6,480,082 divided by the Issuer's fully diluted shares immediately prior to the Qualified Transaction, subject to price-based anti-dilution adjustment. Principal and 10% accrued interest are convertible. Because both prices are set by reference to a Qualified Transaction, which has not occurred, the conversion price and the number of underlying shares are not currently determinable.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F8">The April 10, 2026 Promissory Note matured on October 10, 2026 and remains outstanding.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F9">Each share of Series C Convertible Preferred Stock is convertible at the holder's option, at any time, into 0.01% of the Issuer's Common Stock on a fully diluted basis at the time of conversion, so the 1,250 shares held by MCC convert into 12.5% of the fully diluted Common Stock. The conversion price and the number of underlying shares vary with the Issuer's capitalization and share price. The Series C Preferred Stock has no expiration date. These shares were reported in Table I of the Form 3 filed October 24, 2025 and are reported in Table II here to reflect their convertible nature.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

    <remarks>This amendment restates in its entirety the reporting person's Form 4 filed October 23, 2026 (accession no. 0001096906-26-001612) in order to (i) include footnotes 1 through 6, which were omitted from the original filing, (ii) attach each footnote to the correct line and column, and (iii) update the reporting person's address. No transaction, amount or holding reported in the original filing is changed. The original Form 4 was filed late; it reported transactions on December 8, 2025, April 10, 2026, May 19, 2026 and May 27, 2026 that were required to be reported within two business days of each transaction. All share amounts reflect the Issuer's 1-for-250 reverse stock split effective June 12, 2026 (exempt under Rule 16a-9).</remarks>

